1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:01,867
<i> Berdugo, how are you, my dear?</i>

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:02,900
<i> I'm all set for my trip.</i>

3
00:00:03,033 --> 00:00:03,833
<i> And the sample?</i>

4
00:00:03,967 --> 00:00:05,467
<i>Ready.
You won't be disappointed.</i>

5
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,200
<i>Well, I'll see you soon,
my dear.</i>

6
00:00:07,333 --> 00:00:09,833
<i>So your theory is that Berdugo
will replace Godfather</i>

7
00:00:09,967 --> 00:00:11,533
<i>as the supplier here in Valmora.</i>

8
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:13,600
<i>Seems like it,
that's why I came to you.</i>

9
00:00:13,733 --> 00:00:15,900
<i>Why did you even need
to come here to Valmora?</i>

10
00:00:16,033 --> 00:00:17,433
<i> To accompany Joey?</i>

11
00:00:17,567 --> 00:00:18,867
<i> You're such a good friend.</i>

12
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,833
<i> And a dedicated Journalist.</i>

13
00:00:20,967 --> 00:00:23,967
<i>Just remember, posture, calm,
eye contact.</i>

14
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:25,367
<i>She will notice the difference.</i>

15
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,767
<i>Do you need all this
just to get her attention?</i>

16
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:30,633
<i>You're a good guy, Peter.
You will be good for Joey.</i>

17
00:00:30,767 --> 00:00:31,700
<i> Last one!</i>

18
00:00:33,167 --> 00:00:34,733
<i>You can stay here as long
as you need.</i>

19
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:36,100
<i> Thanks, Zoey.</i>

20
00:00:36,233 --> 00:00:37,300
<i> No problem.</i>

21
00:00:37,433 --> 00:00:39,733
<i>Andrew, can I talk to you
just for a moment?</i>

22
00:00:39,867 --> 00:00:43,000
<i>Joey is pretty.
Maybe you're doing this to...</i>

23
00:00:43,133 --> 00:00:45,033
<i> to help my friend.</i>

24
00:00:45,167 --> 00:00:45,900
<i> Joey, my child...</i>

25
00:00:46,033 --> 00:00:47,800
<i> Father, I'm right.</i>

26
00:00:47,933 --> 00:00:50,133
<i>You're the guy I was following
earlier.</i>

27
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:52,833
<i>How did that happen?
Didn't your car burn down?</i>

28
00:00:52,967 --> 00:00:54,167
<i> Long story, my child.</i>

29
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:55,300
<i> Bro, I'll go ahead.</i>

30
00:00:55,433 --> 00:00:56,400
<i> Are you leaving now?</i>

31
00:00:56,533 --> 00:00:58,267
<i>I'm sorry I didn't tell you
that I moved.</i>

32
00:00:58,400 --> 00:00:59,400
<i> Where?</i>

33
00:00:59,533 --> 00:01:00,967
<i>Somewhere closer to where
Theresa might be.</i>

34
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:02,967
<i>Don't worry.
I'm being very careful.</i>

35
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:04,200
<i> Sorry, my child,</i>

36
00:01:04,333 --> 00:01:07,133
<i>but this is the only way I can
be sure you're safe.</i>

37
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:11,000
<i>I'll bring down the syndicate.
No one can know I'm alive.</i>

38
00:01:11,133 --> 00:01:11,867
<i> Not even Andrew?</i>

39
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,267
<i> Joey, who are you talking to?</i>

40
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:15,500
<i> Mother.</i>

41
00:01:34,367 --> 00:01:37,200
She's not here.
I haven't seen Joey yet.

42
00:01:38,333 --> 00:01:41,767
And she didn't tell me
she was coming here.

43
00:01:41,933 --> 00:01:45,200
But okay, I'll let you know
when she suddenly arrives.

44
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:03,333
What happened to your face
of the night look?

45
00:02:03,467 --> 00:02:06,100
Nothing, I just thought of Joey.

46
00:02:06,233 --> 00:02:08,433
She didn't even tell me
she was coming home.

47
00:02:08,567 --> 00:02:09,967
Why would she tell you?

48
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:12,500
Are you her boyfriend
to inform you?

49
00:02:12,633 --> 00:02:14,767
- What?
- Joke!

50
00:02:14,933 --> 00:02:15,967
Just a joke.

51
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:18,967
You're getting angry again.
You're overly serious.

52
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:22,233
You know the situation
with our friend, right?

53
00:02:22,367 --> 00:02:23,800
She lost someone.

54
00:02:23,933 --> 00:02:26,067
I'm not sulking, okay?

55
00:02:27,533 --> 00:02:29,433
I was just worried about her.

56
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:33,167
I want to comfort her, but how?
I don't know where she is.

57
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:36,367
She didn't say if she was coming
here or not.

58
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:42,367
Here.

59
00:02:43,667 --> 00:02:45,833
There are only two rooms
in the house, which means...

60
00:02:45,967 --> 00:02:49,167
Which means I'll sleep here in
the living room, on the sofa.

61
00:02:50,233 --> 00:02:50,900
Okay.

62
00:02:52,767 --> 00:02:56,833
The bed is ready in that room.
You can sleep there tonight.

63
00:02:56,967 --> 00:02:58,167
Thanks, Zoey.

64
00:02:59,267 --> 00:03:01,567
I'm going to rest, okay?
I'm tired.

65
00:03:01,700 --> 00:03:03,867
Good night, Joey.

66
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,867
You're so obvious.

67
00:03:21,567 --> 00:03:22,667
Obvious?

68
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:25,000
What do you mean?

69
00:03:25,133 --> 00:03:27,767
It's obvious to you
that you like Joey.

70
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:31,267
I'm just concerned
about my friend.

71
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:33,767
Really?

72
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:38,467
Because I remember you used
to look at me that way.

73
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:40,000
When we were still together.

74
00:03:41,667 --> 00:03:44,000
I remember that look.

75
00:03:44,133 --> 00:03:46,100
I know that look.

76
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:50,900
Good night, Andrew.

77
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,933
<i>The number you dialed
is unattended.</i>

78
00:04:18,067 --> 00:04:19,533
<i> Please try your call...</i>

79
00:04:29,467 --> 00:04:30,900
You want some jam, Mom?

80
00:04:32,267 --> 00:04:34,133
No. No, thank you, my child.

81
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:38,267
Hon, good morning.

82
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:39,267
Let's have breakfast.

83
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,733
No. I'll take care of something.

84
00:04:42,867 --> 00:04:44,167
Good morning, Mom.

85
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:45,533
Good morning.

86
00:04:47,133 --> 00:04:50,267
It seems like you have
an early appointment.

87
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:52,567
Time is money, Hon.

88
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:56,100
I need to prepare for my
business meeting in a few days.

89
00:04:56,233 --> 00:04:57,867
Which reminds me,

90
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,900
I won't be home
for the next few days.

91
00:05:01,533 --> 00:05:03,367
It looks like your appointment
is important.

92
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:04,733
Do you want me to come lwith
you?

93
00:05:04,867 --> 00:05:05,933
No need, Hon.

94
00:05:06,067 --> 00:05:07,967
You'll just get bored.

95
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:10,900
Anyway, we'll just celebrate
when I come home.

96
00:05:11,033 --> 00:05:14,167
Wow, this looks like big time,
Hon.

97
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:15,333
Okay.

98
00:05:15,467 --> 00:05:18,500
I know you'll be successful
no matter what you do.

99
00:05:18,633 --> 00:05:20,633
Of course, you know me.

100
00:05:20,767 --> 00:05:22,567
I always get what I want.

101
00:05:26,767 --> 00:05:27,700
Mom!

102
00:05:31,433 --> 00:05:32,367
Are you okay?

103
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:33,467
Yeah.

104
00:05:34,567 --> 00:05:38,100
I'm okay, I'm okay.
I'll just go back to my room.

105
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:41,067
Help her.

106
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:43,400
No, I can do it.

107
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:49,533
I told you not to help me!
Don't you understand!

108
00:05:49,667 --> 00:05:52,833
Mom, she was just trying
to help you!

109
00:06:02,833 --> 00:06:04,533
Has she taken her meds?

110
00:06:04,667 --> 00:06:06,367
She looks like she's having
a meltdown.

111
00:06:14,867 --> 00:06:17,200
<i>Mom's moods are changing again.</i>

112
00:06:17,333 --> 00:06:19,667
<i>Maybe she needs a change
of meds.</i>

113
00:06:22,533 --> 00:06:23,500
Are you okay?

114
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:28,133
It's my Mommy.

115
00:06:28,267 --> 00:06:30,600
My sister said she is having
mood swings again.

116
00:06:32,233 --> 00:06:33,467
<i> Just go home.</i>

117
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:35,100
<i> Be with your Mother.</i>

118
00:06:35,233 --> 00:06:38,633
<i>Tell her you talked to me
and I'm alive.</i>

119
00:06:38,767 --> 00:06:40,767
Maybe you need to go home?

120
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:42,933
It's okay if they're looking
for you.

121
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:44,533
I'll go with you and come home.

122
00:06:46,633 --> 00:06:48,933
No, it's okay.
My sister's there.

123
00:06:49,067 --> 00:06:50,600
I'll just ask for updates.

124
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:53,033
Let's continue this.

125
00:06:57,900 --> 00:06:58,867
Zoey?

126
00:07:00,767 --> 00:07:04,533
Are you sure about the one we're
waiting for?

127
00:07:04,667 --> 00:07:05,400
Yes.

128
00:07:05,533 --> 00:07:07,033
He's been my asset
for a long time.

129
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:16,867
He's here.

130
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,200
Who are you with?

131
00:07:20,333 --> 00:07:21,633
My friends.

132
00:07:21,767 --> 00:07:23,600
These guys are okay.

133
00:07:23,733 --> 00:07:25,100
What's the news
about drugs here?

134
00:07:25,233 --> 00:07:27,200
Customers are coming
from everywhere.

135
00:07:27,333 --> 00:07:30,333
The drugs have been running out
since Godfather disappeared.

136
00:07:30,467 --> 00:07:32,867
That's why there's
no one supplying.

137
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,100
Hasn't a new supplier come in?

138
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:41,867
Maybe you've heard a new name,
it's Berdugo.

139
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,300
Berdugo?

140
00:07:43,433 --> 00:07:45,467
This is the first time
I heard that name.

141
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:55,200
Excuse me.

142
00:08:00,067 --> 00:08:01,133
Hello, Mom?

143
00:08:01,267 --> 00:08:02,533
My child, Joey...

144
00:08:02,667 --> 00:08:06,633
Are you back in your dorm?
You didn't inform me.

145
00:08:06,767 --> 00:08:08,233
<i> Sorry, Mother.</i>

146
00:08:08,367 --> 00:08:12,000
I was really tired and fell
asleep last night.

147
00:08:12,133 --> 00:08:14,800
That's why you and Peter
haven't seen each other, right?

148
00:08:14,933 --> 00:08:15,933
<i> Peter?</i>

149
00:08:16,067 --> 00:08:18,667
Yes, we haven't talked.

150
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:27,167
Joey, I'm going to the precinct
to get an update about your dad.

151
00:08:27,333 --> 00:08:31,400
I hope they release the remains
of Miguel.

152
00:08:31,533 --> 00:08:34,233
Mother, if it's about Father,
you don't need to worry.

153
00:08:34,367 --> 00:08:36,000
We don't have any problems
with that anymore.

154
00:08:36,133 --> 00:08:37,100
What?

155
00:08:38,133 --> 00:08:40,033
Why did you say we don't have
any problems

156
00:08:40,167 --> 00:08:42,167
with your father anymore?

157
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:45,333
<i>Father, I'll help you.
It's hard if you're alone.</i>

158
00:08:45,467 --> 00:08:48,533
<i>You'll find Berdugo easier
if you have someone with you.</i>

159
00:08:48,667 --> 00:08:50,967
<i>Father, I just don't want
anything bad to happen to you.</i>

160
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:52,167
<i> My child, don't.</i>

161
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:55,833
<i>Just go home.
Be with your Mother.</i>

162
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:01,367
I mean, don't worry because
you might get sick, Mother.

163
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:04,600
Joey, answer my question first.

164
00:09:04,733 --> 00:09:07,033
Why did you say we won't have
any more problems

165
00:09:07,167 --> 00:09:09,100
with your Father?

166
00:09:09,233 --> 00:09:13,700
Because Father doesn't want us
to think about him.

167
00:09:13,833 --> 00:09:17,233
<i>He wants us to just get on
with our lives.</i>

168
00:09:17,367 --> 00:09:18,567
That's why I'll do it,

169
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:21,167
even though it hurts me
that Father is gone,

170
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:23,633
I'll just take care
of the things I need to do

171
00:09:23,767 --> 00:09:24,933
here in the dorm.

172
00:09:25,067 --> 00:09:27,867
Go ahead and finish everything
so you can come home soon.

173
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:30,467
Love you, Joey.

174
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:32,200
I love you, Mom.

175
00:09:39,467 --> 00:09:41,533
<i>Sorry, Father,
if I don't obey you.</i>

176
00:09:41,667 --> 00:09:43,867
<i>I know you need my help
more now.</i>

177
00:09:48,333 --> 00:09:50,233
I want to know who
that Berdugo is.

178
00:09:51,833 --> 00:09:53,800
Just as soon as you get
any information about him,

179
00:09:53,933 --> 00:09:55,300
let me know right away.

180
00:09:55,433 --> 00:09:57,100
Okay, Ma'am.

181
00:09:57,233 --> 00:09:58,267
All right,
I'll take care of that.

182
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,533
All right.

183
00:10:01,300 --> 00:10:03,233
Mister, as soon as you
have any information,

184
00:10:03,367 --> 00:10:04,467
let me know, okay?

185
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:06,100
I'll give you a free snack.

186
00:10:06,233 --> 00:10:06,967
Promise me that, Ma'am, okay?

187
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:08,300
Promise.

188
00:10:10,633 --> 00:10:11,633
Come on, let's go.

189
00:10:11,767 --> 00:10:12,800
Let's go.

190
00:10:32,467 --> 00:10:33,800
Sir...

191
00:10:33,933 --> 00:10:37,400
Hey, it seems like you're doing
something stupid again.

192
00:10:37,567 --> 00:10:40,067
Sir, you're being suspicious
again.

193
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:42,833
Someone is just asking
for some help.

194
00:10:42,967 --> 00:10:45,867
They're asking if I know
anything about Berdugo.

195
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,333
Do you know him, Sir?

196
00:10:47,467 --> 00:10:49,333
No. I don't know Berdugo.

197
00:10:49,467 --> 00:10:54,100
Hey, you, get out of my sight.
I might arrest you. Get out!

198
00:10:54,233 --> 00:10:55,367
Yes, Sir.

199
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:10,133
Hello? Why are you calling?
Is there a problem?

200
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:13,867
Sir, someone is asking about
Berdugo.

201
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,200
<i>That's our boss's name,
right, Sir?</i>

202
00:11:16,333 --> 00:11:18,467
Find out who's looking
for Berdugo.

203
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:20,800
Okay, Sir, I'll take care of it.

204
00:11:20,933 --> 00:11:22,300
I'll find out.

205
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:39,167
<i> Hello, Peter?</i>

206
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:40,300
Joey!

207
00:11:40,433 --> 00:11:42,200
It's good I finally talked
to you. Where are you?

208
00:11:42,367 --> 00:11:45,033
Your Mother is looking for you.
She's worried about you.

209
00:11:45,167 --> 00:11:46,800
<i> I talked to Mother already.</i>

210
00:11:46,933 --> 00:11:49,867
<i> Okay, don't worry.</i>

211
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,733
But where are you now?

212
00:11:51,867 --> 00:11:53,900
<i>Andrew and I are following
a lead.</i>

213
00:11:54,033 --> 00:11:55,600
<i> We're here in Valmora.</i>

214
00:11:56,800 --> 00:12:00,233
<i> Someone is helping us,
so we're okay here, we're safe.</i>

215
00:12:00,367 --> 00:12:02,700
<i>I'll just call you
when we get back to Manila.</i>

216
00:12:02,833 --> 00:12:05,033
<i> Sorry, we're just busy here.</i>

217
00:12:13,967 --> 00:12:15,467
Here.

218
00:12:15,633 --> 00:12:17,167
Maybe you haven't had
your coffee yet.

219
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:19,000
We left early.

220
00:12:21,733 --> 00:12:22,833
Thank you.

221
00:12:31,233 --> 00:12:32,200
Delicious.

222
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:34,867
Of course.

223
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:38,033
I still remember how you like
your coffee.

224
00:12:38,167 --> 00:12:40,300
I remember a lot of things,
you know.

225
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:44,900
Are you still angry about
what happened to us before?

226
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:49,833
No, where did you suddenly pull
that out?

227
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,233
Andrew, it's been a while.

228
00:12:52,367 --> 00:12:53,933
Let's not talk about it.

229
00:12:54,067 --> 00:12:55,900
You know, just enjoy your coffee

230
00:12:56,033 --> 00:12:58,700
because I'm the only one
who can do that.

231
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:09,800
I hope your informant
gets some news.

232
00:13:09,933 --> 00:13:13,667
Because at this point,
I feel like we're on a dead end.

233
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:17,800
Unless you have something
to share.

234
00:13:19,567 --> 00:13:22,133
There's this woman
under my radar,

235
00:13:22,300 --> 00:13:23,400
it's Delilah.

236
00:13:23,533 --> 00:13:25,600
She's the one I'm working on
right now.

237
00:13:25,733 --> 00:13:30,100
She's my current target
because she's the one suspected

238
00:13:30,233 --> 00:13:31,767
of being in charge of drug
distribution here in Valmora.

239
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:35,933
You know, if Berdugo is meeting
someone here, it might be her.

240
00:13:37,167 --> 00:13:38,200
That's good.

241
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:44,267
You know, I'm having a hard time
catching Delilah.

242
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:47,367
because I don't have any
evidence against her yet.

243
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:50,033
So my plan is to get close
to her.

244
00:13:50,167 --> 00:13:52,600
She has a lot of businesses here
in Valmora.

245
00:13:52,733 --> 00:13:55,833
One of them is the new
Nature Hotel and Resort.

246
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:59,667
What I heard is that she's
staying there now.

247
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:02,867
Okay, I'll check in there
to investigate.

248
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,367
Andrew, don't.

249
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:07,667
It's my job to go undercover,

250
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,867
so I should be the one
to do that.

251
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,500
Zoey, we can do this together.

252
00:14:12,633 --> 00:14:15,500
- I'll help you.
- That's even worse!

253
00:14:15,633 --> 00:14:17,867
Your face is too recognizable,
Andrew.

254
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:19,933
And if they see you
at the resort,

255
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:22,533
the people there might be
alerted.

256
00:14:22,667 --> 00:14:25,667
You know, I'll just come back
here to update you.

257
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:29,200
If I get any information
about Berdugo, okay?

258
00:14:35,667 --> 00:14:36,567
Andrew.

259
00:14:38,867 --> 00:14:41,167
I know you, okay?

260
00:14:42,433 --> 00:14:45,467
But please, just do what I say?

261
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:48,067
Just stay put.

262
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:49,800
I'll take care of it.

263
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:55,633
I'm leaving.

264
00:15:07,167 --> 00:15:09,867
Mom, take your medicine first,
okay?

265
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:14,533
Why did you bring that?
Where's the caregiver?

266
00:15:19,033 --> 00:15:22,700
She left already, Mom.
Sorry, I couldn't stop her.

267
00:15:22,833 --> 00:15:25,800
Because she was shocked
by what you did, Mom.

268
00:15:27,367 --> 00:15:31,567
She's very sensitive.
She should just leave.

269
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:36,100
She didn't do anything wrong.

270
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:42,867
Mom, how many caregivers have
left here because of you?

271
00:15:45,533 --> 00:15:47,233
Is there a problem, Mom?

272
00:15:48,633 --> 00:15:50,500
Maybe you want to talk about it.

273
00:15:50,633 --> 00:15:52,033
Just tell me.

274
00:15:58,233 --> 00:16:02,733
How can I help you if you
don't tell me the problem?

275
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:16,433
Andrew...

276
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:21,933
I heard your conversation
with Zoey.

277
00:16:22,067 --> 00:16:24,867
So what now?
Is it really a dead end for us?

278
00:16:26,033 --> 00:16:29,600
When did that even stop us
from making a plan?

279
00:16:30,667 --> 00:16:34,667
Has "Joey On Duty" lost her
courage?

280
00:16:38,867 --> 00:16:44,433
What if Delilah is really
the one Berdugo came here for?

281
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:47,500
And if we're able to confirm
that theory,

282
00:16:48,833 --> 00:16:52,533
then we can set him up,
and we can expose him.

283
00:16:52,667 --> 00:16:54,000
And we can bring justice

284
00:16:54,133 --> 00:16:56,133
to everything he did
to my family.

285
00:16:56,267 --> 00:16:57,733
Yes,

286
00:16:57,867 --> 00:17:01,133
and if your father is alive

287
00:17:01,267 --> 00:17:08,067
and if he needs help when he's
facing Berdugo, we'll be there.

288
00:17:09,300 --> 00:17:11,200
Okay, I'm game.

289
00:17:11,333 --> 00:17:12,967
But what are we going to do?

290
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:18,400
Actually, I've already thought
of something.

291
00:17:18,533 --> 00:17:19,867
But, I don't know if you'll
agree.

292
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:21,267
I hope you will.

293
00:17:22,300 --> 00:17:23,567
Why? What is that?

294
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:29,333
Everything is ready for
your guest's arrival,

295
00:17:29,467 --> 00:17:30,900
Madam Delilah.

296
00:17:31,033 --> 00:17:32,900
Are you sure, Francis?

297
00:17:33,033 --> 00:17:34,167
Yes, Madam.

298
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:36,933
I even had a meeting with
the resort staff

299
00:17:37,067 --> 00:17:40,400
to make sure they would give
the guest VIP treatment.

300
00:17:40,533 --> 00:17:41,700
It should be.

301
00:17:41,833 --> 00:17:43,600
I don't want to be embarrassed.

302
00:17:43,733 --> 00:17:48,500
If this deal goes South,
I will lose a lot,

303
00:17:50,733 --> 00:17:52,733
and you will lose too.

304
00:17:52,867 --> 00:17:54,633
Madam, that won't happen.

305
00:18:59,433 --> 00:19:00,533
Hi.

306
00:19:00,667 --> 00:19:02,167
I would like to get a room,
please.

307
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:04,500
Okay, Ma'am.
Are you with someone?

308
00:19:04,633 --> 00:19:07,667
I wish, but I'm alone.

309
00:19:10,167 --> 00:19:13,200
You need to tighten security
here at the hotel.

310
00:19:13,333 --> 00:19:16,167
I don't want to put my deal
with Berdugo at risk.

311
00:19:17,267 --> 00:19:18,300
Yes, Madam.

312
00:19:18,433 --> 00:19:19,933
I already assigned someone.

313
00:19:20,067 --> 00:19:21,233
Good.

314
00:19:35,967 --> 00:19:37,300
Boss Delilah,

315
00:19:37,433 --> 00:19:41,200
I'm sorry if I burned the money
from what was sold.

316
00:19:42,300 --> 00:19:44,133
I got carried away.

317
00:19:44,267 --> 00:19:46,767
I'll just pay you right away.

318
00:19:46,900 --> 00:19:49,700
You know I don't like being
fooled.

319
00:19:49,833 --> 00:19:52,200
What will happen to my business

320
00:19:52,333 --> 00:19:55,167
if my people keep outsmarting
me?

321
00:19:55,300 --> 00:19:57,967
Give me another chance.

322
00:19:58,100 --> 00:19:59,900
I'll give you your money back
right away!

323
00:20:00,033 --> 00:20:01,633
I'll find a way!

324
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:05,133
You should have done
that a long time ago.

325
00:20:05,267 --> 00:20:06,867
- I'm sorry.
- Boss...

326
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:10,833
Because if one does it,
everyone will do it.

327
00:20:10,967 --> 00:20:11,933
Boss...

328
00:20:12,067 --> 00:20:13,667
Boss, have mercy on me, Boss!

329
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:14,800
Boss...

330
00:20:25,467 --> 00:20:28,267
- Beautiful, isn't it?
- Wow, it's beautiful here!

331
00:20:28,400 --> 00:20:31,700
- Of course. Yes?
- Wait. Let's take a picture.

332
00:20:31,833 --> 00:20:33,000
Okay, okay.

333
00:21:03,900 --> 00:21:06,433
Something's going through
my daughter's mind.

334
00:21:06,567 --> 00:21:08,800
Chief, she has a feeling
that Miguel is still alive.

335
00:21:08,967 --> 00:21:11,267
I'm begging you.
Just a little more patience.

336
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:12,500
Thank you, Chief.

337
00:21:12,633 --> 00:21:14,867
I might not be able to take care
of my foundation anymore.

338
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:17,267
Mom lost her caregiver.

339
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:20,100
Ma'am, if you can't find anyone,
I can.

340
00:21:20,233 --> 00:21:24,133
That guy in red,
he called Delilah his boss.

341
00:21:24,267 --> 00:21:27,833
I feel like we can get better
results if we work together,

342
00:21:27,967 --> 00:21:28,867
Zoey.

343
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:29,767
Boss, they seem to be getting
suspicious.

344
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:31,100
So that there won't be any
problems,

345
00:21:31,233 --> 00:21:32,800
I'll meet with Delilah.

346
00:21:32,933 --> 00:21:35,967
Hello there!
I didn't know I had a neighbor.

347
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:37,067
I'm Madam Delilah.

348
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:38,333
I'm Joey.
